<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Marius the Younger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">110–82 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-marius">Gaius Marius</a> the Younger was a Roman politician, the son, probably by adoption, of the general Gaius Marius. Elected consul in 82 BCE at about 27 during the civil war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a>, he was defeated at Sacriportus and besieged in Praeneste, where he killed himself as the town fell.</p></div>
